For most elements, any program will compute a default x and y position. The position attributes let this be changed two ways.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"name":"placement","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The placement attribute indicates whether something is above or below another element, such as a note or a notation.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"name":"orientation","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The orientation attribute indicates whether slurs and ties are overhand (tips down) or underhand (tips up). This is distinct from the placement attribute used by any notation type.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"name":"bezierX","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The x-coordinate, in tenths relative to any position settings, of the outgoing bezier control point for a slur or tie with a start type, or the incoming control point for one with a stop or continue type.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"name":"bezierY","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The y-coordinate, in tenths relative to any position settings, of the outgoing bezier control point for a slur or tie with a start type, or the incoming control point for one with a stop or continue type.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"name":"bezierX2","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The x-coordinate, in tenths, of the outgoing bezier control point for a slur with a continue type.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"name":"bezierY2","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The y-coordinate, in tenths, of the outgoing bezier control point for a slur with a continue type.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"name":"bezierOffset","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The outgoing bezier control point offset, in musical divisions, for a slur or tie with a start type, or the incoming control point offset for one with a stop or continue type. Deprecated as of MusicXML 3.1 in favor of ","type":"text"},{"code":"bezierX","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"name":"bezierOffset2","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The outgoing bezier control point offset, in musical divisions, for a slur with a continue type. Deprecated as of MusicXML 3.1 in favor of ","type":"text"},{"code":"bezierX2","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"name":"color","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The color attribute group indicates the color of an element.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"kind":"parameters"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTied\/init(id:kind:number:lineKind:dashLength:spaceLength:position:placement:orientation:bezierX:bezierY:bezierX2:bezierY2:bezierOffset:bezierOffset2:color:)"},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"title":"init(id:kind:number:lineKind:dashLength:spaceLength:position:placement:orientation:bezierX:bezierY:bezierX2:bezierY2:bezierOffset:bezierOffset2:color:)","roleHeading":"Initializer","externalID":"s:7IvorMXL7MXLTiedV2id4kind6number8lineKind10dashLength05spaceJ08position9placement11orientation7bezierX0O1Y0O2X20O2Y20O6Offset0O7Offset25colorACSSSg_AC0H0OAA14MXLNumberLevelVSgAA07MXLLineH0OSgSdSgA1_AA11MXLPositionVAA13MXLAboveBelowOSgAA12MXLOverUnderOSgA1_A1_A1_A1_AA12MXLDivisionsVSgA12_AA8MXLColorVSgtcfc","role":"symbol","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"init"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"id"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"kind":"text","text":"?, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"kind"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Kind","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL7MXLTiedV4KindO"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"number"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLNumberLevel","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL14MXLNum